course: dictionary
lesson: 15484
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and «stripped» is one of them. You can work out which meaning is right by reading the words around it, which are its context. «We stripped the old paint off the door.» Paint is a covering, so stripped means took off a layer.
explain: «The referee stripped the player of his title for cheating.» The words of his title and for cheating tell you that stripped here means taken away from someone, as a punishment. The same word can mean something very different in a different sentence.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If took off a layer fits the paint but not the title, you have chosen the right meaning for each sentence. Stripped can also describe something bare: «The stripped wood was pale and smooth.»
fact: Stripped is the past form of the verb strip: strip, strips, stripped, stripping.
fact: «Stripped» can mean took off a covering or layer, such as paint, bark or sheets.
fact: «Stripped» can mean took off your clothes.
fact: «Stripped of» something means it was taken away from someone, often as a punishment.
fact: As an adjective, «stripped» means bare, with the cover taken off, as in «stripped wood».
exercise: «We stripped the beds to wash the sheets.» What does stripped mean here? | Folded them into a box | *Took off the covers | Painted them | Made them very tidy
exercise: «The athlete was stripped of his medal for cheating.» What does stripped of mean? | Put on a new uniform | Lost his shoes | Was given a bigger prize | *Had something taken away as a punishment
exercise: «The winter wind stripped the trees bare.» What does stripped bare suggest? | *Their leaves were blown off, leaving them bare | They were given new coats | They grew taller overnight | They were painted bright green
test: «Dad stripped the old varnish off the table.» Which meaning of stripped fits? | Was given a big prize | Painted in bright colours | Took off his shoes and socks | *Took off a layer
test: «The stripped copper wire was ready to join the circuit.» What does stripped mean in this sentence? | *Bare, with the plastic cover taken off | Coated in bright paint | Hidden inside a box | Twisted into a knot
exam: Which sentence uses stripped to mean taken away as a punishment? | *The judge stripped him of his driving licence | The stripped floor shone in the sun | The sailors stripped the ship's sails for repairs | She stripped off her wet coat
